From 4172d7dce396478609201c20ea346c824f72b163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niri-RDP rebase <niri-rdp@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:54:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] tests: remote input regressions for the Niri-RDP bridge
 contract

Client-server tests of the virtual keyboard and pointer behaviour the
Niri-RDP bridge relies on. Most of it is now provided by upstream niri
and Smithay (features F7, F9 and F11 of the old private patch); F8 and
F10 are covered by the two previous patches:

- a device that sends the seat keymap back reaches niri binds (Mod+D) and
  the focused window without a keymap swap (F7);
- a no_keymap device follows a layout reload;
- the modifiers sync keeps a layout switched by a niri bind and applies
  CapsLock (F8);
- the committed Unicode device (keycodes "niri_rdp_unicode", key 247,
  NUL-terminated file) commits the exact character and the seat keymap,
  layout and CapsLock are restored afterwards (F10);
- the same with an input method that relays the text keymap and keys
  late: the focused client decodes the exact text and the seat returns
  to the configured keymap (F10/F11);
- destroying the devices releases held keys and restores the keymap (F9);
- sealed and unsealed keymap files, with or without a trailing NUL, are
  accepted;
- keys an input method (Fcitx) forwards through its own virtual keyboard
  bypass its grab and do not update XKB again (no double CapsLock, F11);
- wheel notches sent as axis_discrete reach Mod+WheelScrollDown binds as
  v120, partial notches do not.
